From: phoenix port <fix@me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix: add ramoops node

Debug-only, fully revertible (delete this patch and rebuild).

Reserve the same 1 MiB region at 0xbff00000 that stock MIUI uses for its
ramoops backend (verified against the stock Android boot DTBs), so nothing
else claims it across cold and warm boots. Warm resets do not clear DRAM,
so this captures the kernel console tail from before a hard reset with zero
kernel log - the forensics channel for the recurring ~40s boot loop.

- console-size 0x40000: kernel printk tail (the crash evidence)
- record-size  0x20000: oops/die records
- pmsg-size    0x20000: /dev/pmsg0 userspace canary ring
- ecc-size 16: Reed-Solomon ECC per 128-byte block; without it the reserved
  DRAM bit-flips and the crash text comes out garbled (2026-08-26 evidence
  was ~50% corrupt). Adds ~0x8000 of parity, still fits the 1 MiB region.

Read evidence after reboot from /sys/fs/pstore/ (systemd-pstore.service
archives it under /var/lib/systemd/pstore/).

Signed-off-by: phoenix port <fix@me>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts
@@ -69,6 +69,16 @@
 			qcom,client-id = <1>;
 			qcom,vmid = <QCOM_SCM_VMID_MSS_MSA>;
 		};
+
+		ramoops_mem: ramoops@bff00000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0xbff00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+			no-map;
+		};
 	};
 };
 
